{"login": "piotrcurious", "location": null, "commits": [{"sha": "cf6ab700c2f4c09b589c4bffce259702a4053f10", "message": "Update taskfun3.ino", "created_at": "2023-11-18T22:59:14Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b2f2cd11cb7540a209739dfa30631884112bb2ff", "message": "Update taskfun3.ino\n\nsyncvar", "created_at": "2023-11-18T22:55:16Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "64e876af189fa4e7b41cb20952c53743941c2f19", "message": "Update taskfun3.ino", "created_at": "2023-11-18T22:47:11Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "11349591e943d8377bfaef0827dd22f20c6770af", "message": "Update taskfun3.ino", "created_at": "2023-11-18T22:40:25Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b6094a65ea387f9c1eb0a1e4df2b3bd6f3cb3807", "message": "Create taskfun3.ino", "created_at": "2023-11-18T20:33:44Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "571864a6854b250d995cd4240b9654caabad08dc", "message": "Create taskfun2.ino\n\ncontains bugs in updating estimates", "created_at": "2023-11-18T20:25:54Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c1e802ff8406b10c05b32553580b7ebd5be83e5e", "message": "Create Readme.md", "created_at": "2023-11-18T20:24:55Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "69716c002876f24f00f6393de5b8cc5c5b86eb76", "message": "Create new_taskfun_overhaul.ino\n\nNew idea to use taskfun for reading the sensors.", "created_at": "2023-11-18T20:15:42Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "49da9cf972ef27423b81768c8c2bd28efb5d01b4", "message": "Bug fixes\n\n-Better noise reduction of low magnitude Tslopes\r\n-improved capacity_in accountancy by integrating method \r\n-other smaller fixes", "created_at": "2021-11-22T23:23:18Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "6e13e9c97653dddb6f62a3cb95077409d3978a96", "message": "Added more visuals for TVTerminal\n\nas TVTerminal ( https://www.serasidis.gr/circuits/TV_terminal/Small_TV_terminal.htm )\r\nsupports 40x25 text AND 2x3 semigraphics, \r\nit is possible to create nice plots in 80x75 resolution! \r\nOnly problem was - with serial TX only terminal, it is not possible to read character from the screen to merge plot data.\r\nI solved it by creating small ring buffer, rembering recent plot(x,y) data. This is not perfect solution, \r\nbut works good enough. \r\nEnjoy.", "created_at": "2021-11-21T02:01:01Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "424e0e0f3393d1c8833ea3c321d371af036542b0", "message": "added IR modulated serial display", "created_at": "2021-11-18T19:49:34Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "fa7ffadee14465550fa2048b18f7c7b821a4fbf8", "message": "Added display over SoftwareSerial_IR\n\nD13 emits IR software serial data to use with f.e. TVTerm \r\n36khz, 1200baud. \r\nconnect IR transmit diode to D13 (via 100ohm), connect two in series if You want larger range. \r\nconnect IR demodulator to TTL serial port of terminal.\r\ncode has option to use VT100 , default is TVTerm, as in https://www.serasidis.gr/circuits/TV_terminal/Small_TV_terminal.htm\r\nit has different control codes. \r\nchange to VT100 to use \"real\" serial terminal.", "created_at": "2021-11-18T19:38:35Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2c6175f6b7bd5e0029d41f8928f9d9bec50b0a04", "message": "added dual thermistor version\n\nThis version uses charges single battery. \r\nIt uses dual thermistor setup - two for battery and two for ambient temp.\r\nTemperature is averaged, reducing influence of ADC noise, drift, etc. \r\nit uses two layers of kalman filter, but it's still simple kalman so no proper model or nonlinearity is factored in. \r\n\r\nThis is work in progress and in theory dual channel operation should be still supported, still it's brutally chopped off here and there. \r\nSo far I've noticed that one channel influences readings of the other via supply voltage.\r\nIn future I plan to develop version not reading voltages at all (maybe only current) , and using transistor on minus side of battery \r\nVoltage reading is not really usefull for charging, temperature is enough. \r\nTransistor on minus side allows better protection against reverse polarity battery insertion. \r\n\r\nThis version is transition version, done quickly because I have no time for it yet, but I needed reliable device to charge small batteries. \r\nIt works very good . \r\nSome hacks are implemented to double sensitivity - theshold of Tslope (over 0.005 , set in weird place in code)\r\nAlso stabilisation period at start of charge got improved - not only Tslope is muted, but also dT is silenced during period of fan spinning and equalising temperature. \r\nIt still uses old circuit, though I updated this sketch to different values of components . They are not optimal - just found in junk box. \r\n\r\nAlso added voltage debug - use it to tune Your voltage divider for Vbat , and Vcc constant  - just throw any resistors and Vcc voltage regulator,\r\nthen connect decent voltmeter to measure voltage on A0 and A1 pins and voila. \r\nYou need to adjust pwm_level in the debug code directly - sorry. In future it will react to knob position to make things easier. \r\n\r\nAlso note NTC skew code is bit iffy, I usually lock up KALMAN_AUTOSKEW_FREEZE and probe values by hand - otherwise it oscillates too much. \r\nif You manage to go below 0.5C temp difference (10bit ADC is Really the limit) it's good. \r\nIn future i'll add better code to probe thermistors without ADC - bit banging to discharge and measure rate of charge of capacitor. \r\nIt is way slower, but seems only sane method to go down 16bit of resolution and THEN trying to filter out noise.", "created_at": "2021-07-09T19:44:22Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "70f542143a61402d01cd70deb09787206a910aae", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2021-02-23T20:21:35Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "27facd8b3823955ca358dede669e1d35ea80c26e", "message": "initial cooling inertia got dynamic \n\nInitial cooling inertia is defined by timeout . \r\nActually this is a bug, as it creates cross dependency on global timeout and initial cooling. \r\nTODO : fix it.", "created_at": "2021-02-16T17:46:54Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "21138d44c56429e9973d92ac07f76ffdbb24cf44", "message": "Delete 389mAh", "created_at": "2021-02-16T17:45:00Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a1893d052b469ed6e37fa589939be08bb808e272", "message": "Delete 254mAh", "created_at": "2021-02-16T17:44:35Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c811b2b339cd6aff7df3fc5b80f068058ce9c7f9", "message": "added more sample graphs", "created_at": "2021-02-16T17:43:54Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "124dd84e09cce67fd061dfc0f5855b569f11f963", "message": "Create a", "created_at": "2021-02-16T17:42:30Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e5947772c097e5d35b5406584eb639aea1d997fa", "message": "bugfix\n\nfixed bug in disabler of temperature slope averager. \r\n\r\nTODO : make disabler (initial dead time) dynamic , set by end_ts/SWAG", "created_at": "2021-02-14T18:22:03Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "5a5cfd72e959a8fbb02b7a13fad4c63027f64302", "message": "Added \"ambient fan\" feature.\n\n\"ambient fan\" feature adds single, global fan, which starts up on insertion of each battery \r\nequalizing temperatures inside charger battery compartment. \r\nAlong with this feature \"dead time\" was introduced - fan timeout is calculated for each channel, \r\nso this was used as disabling factor for stats collection. \r\nDefaults - 10 minutes of fan/dead time upon each new battery insertion.\r\nTODO : lower Kalman gain during fan spinning , so any thermal shifts get better correlation and thus will not influence\r\ndelta of already running channels.", "created_at": "2021-02-14T18:02:06Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "bca1cc4dfce18fca17ce827e546eb4913661492f", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2021-02-10T14:08:28Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ed9df571c932cab82e3637b85fe2407fc47fefee", "message": "difficult high internal resistance cell", "created_at": "2021-02-09T11:30:54Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7b2e7506c315e85dd765325bc4a94024d6cf8b88", "message": "added sample graph", "created_at": "2021-02-09T03:40:54Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "828fc191f94562d1758e5745e3919e319ea7cc6d", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2021-02-09T00:38:48Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8f8ac976bafa90cb12c8eeaa43bad1bf4888301a", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2021-02-09T00:13:52Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "0ae0a80b0b87b0427a141455728035a1146ff268", "message": "Create README.md", "created_at": "2021-02-09T00:10:40Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "18f5f06644e277ebdc01520dc75ff8f66bcbd5d0", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2021-02-08T19:42:39Z", "repo": "arduino-ni-mh-charger", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4d0dfe09e98982510b52c4146493b0e2e7fd8781", "message": "Add initial dither_fix0_1.ino file with setup", "created_at": "2026-03-29T20:48:02Z", "repo": "engine-cooler-capacity-bargraph", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ddfbd3a40e8d8952acc30aae6ca396e14b2ad580", "message": "Create README.md", "created_at": "2021-02-14T20:12:31Z", "repo": "engine-cooler-capacity-bargraph", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "65a3f0494962e1d02e4847dea12d7aae8cfaf003", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2021-02-14T19:42:03Z", "repo": "engine-cooler-capacity-bargraph", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2f87469142c335e70fd398b05e3e9b131ef9b0db", "message": "New branch with new features\n\nNew features :\r\n-thermal protector by using NTC thermistor on A3 pin \r\n-2nd PWM output , it currently outputs battery level to drive analog battery gauge\r\n-IR serial for debug and remote battery monitoring - too big for attiny13. it could work with attiny85 perhaps?\r\n-divided output by 4 in software to limit max current. new constant added for global output division.", "created_at": "2022-05-24T15:09:46Z", "repo": "attiny-car-fan-control", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ddeaa5700e9f5c4d5425351cbe5730da1434a310", "message": " crude mosfet driver\n\nCrude discrete components mosfet driver, made out of NPN transistors.\r\nTested with 12V supply and 10V threshold mosfet. \r\nIt tends to be stable, but must be built quite compact and with decoupling caps and separate ground path to the mosfet to avoid oscillations if supply voltage sags.\r\nBetter using low level mosfet with the driver for more headroom.\r\nI use it to drive 20A inductive load (fan) with flyback diode mounted on the fan and extra 1000uF on power supply lines made out of several low esr capacitors. \r\nDriver can be tuned easily by adjusting two resistors driving bases from first amplifer (on the left)\r\nIf using large output transistors, like bd139, this might come handy. \r\nWith small bc class 100mA transistors rated up to 100mhz it just works out of the box.", "created_at": "2021-06-07T23:37:30Z", "repo": "attiny-car-fan-control", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b8ea9bbf4837f591791cb9a29093d9011bed72d4", "message": "Create README.md", "created_at": "2021-02-17T22:44:29Z", "repo": "attiny-car-fan-control", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a8ee0636774507889e203f0e296d4a03a8996206", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2021-02-17T21:46:49Z", "repo": "attiny-car-fan-control", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a742f9677f203c0417275c3213022160d5902c50", "message": "Merge pull request #4 from piotrcurious/vibe-test-harness-10968508118702604532\n\nImplement engine simulator test harness and GUI", "created_at": "2026-03-22T01:01:36Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d988a38c48fd2e3dc39705f40d19d280e1f7abfc", "message": "Merge pull request #3 from piotrcurious/vibe-test-harness-10968508118702604532\n\nImplement Engine Simulator Test Harness", "created_at": "2026-03-22T00:36:16Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "94ccca280863c3448529f22a503ef34cb105d9f8", "message": "Create engine.ino", "created_at": "2026-03-22T00:18:44Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d5f03f73ff4859cec07e62fe9e060a35bfeafac5", "message": "Create final_engine_sim4.ino", "created_at": "2026-03-22T00:13:14Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b7e255abfa595d27e1b9508da09306cf839a52ea", "message": "Create final_engine_sim3.ino", "created_at": "2026-03-22T00:07:39Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4d50b041dd17d020d0b1e83bf0bab0d563bb1c89", "message": "Create final_engine_sim2.ino", "created_at": "2026-03-22T00:02:10Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "5dd1b7f28a29da972407c4f3cfd1fd5e23bf16d0", "message": "Merge pull request #2 from piotrcurious/improved-fltk-frontend-10172992150864015045\n\nImproved FLTK Front-end and Tuning for Engine Simulator", "created_at": "2026-03-21T23:47:02Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a458e20cce11d768044eb343f06e5a2b0d6ea0b4", "message": "01vibe", "created_at": "2026-03-21T23:17:45Z", "repo": "arduino-engine-simulator", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "acb86cbf88ef60edc29e156657bd03bf922e21b4", "message": "Merge pull request #1 from piotrcurious/fix/engine-sim-refinement-9519697961699727936